by Kocal at 2026-08-26T15:16:54Z

> On the behaviour changes: there's some BC breaks there, no? But maybe to minor to be realistic?

Indeed we have few changes yes, listed in the PR description, but I don't consider them as a BC:
- We have 3 cases (null, array, BackedEnum) which are now correctly handled instead of throwing an exception ➡️ that's better, also throwing on `null` was a mistake
- And we have these 3 other cases were the rendering changed, but it can't be considered as a BC:

| Attribute value | Before | After |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `true` | `name` | `name=""` |
| `false` on `aria-*` | attribute omitted | `aria-x="false"` |
| `true` on `data-*` | `data-x` | `data-x="true"` |

To resume, the behavior is now identical to what Twig does, and we have less code to maintain 🎉

